  "semantic_difference_list": "input_layout: xtrax needs pre-stacked (n_micro, m, ...) (grad.py:14,59-93); optax reshapes an un-stacked batch with order='F', so microbatch k holds strided rows (_microbatching.py:99,414) || grad_granularity: optax micro_grad takes per-EXAMPLE grads of batch-1 slices via vmap (_microbatching.py:509,644-667); xtrax differentiates the loss over each whole microbatch (grad.py:108-112); equal only for a loss that is a mean of per-example terms || reduction_default: xtrax is always an unweighted mean (grad.py:119-121); optax defaults to SUM (_microbatching.py:564) and needs AccumulationType.MEAN || aux_and_loss_shape: xtrax returns (mean_grads, mean_loss[, mean_aux]) (grad.py:122,127); optax returns (grads, IndividualOutputs(values, metrics, aux)) per example, caller must average (_microbatching.py:34,649-654,662) || non_array_leaves: xtrax uses eqx.filter_value_and_grad (grad.py:108,112); optax uses jax.value_and_grad (_microbatching.py:644) so a callable or int leaf in params raises || uneven_batches: both refuse; optax raises unless batch % microbatch_size == 0 (_microbatching.py:312), xtrax raises on ragged leading or second axis (grad.py:68,90); neither weights by microbatch size || memory_profile: xtrax scan stacks all n_micro gradient trees then means them (grad.py:118-121); optax carries one accumulator through fori_loop but vmaps per-example grads, so a microbatch holds m copies of the gradient tree (_microbatching.py:433-441,509) || reduction_order_and_dtype: xtrax is a pairwise jnp.mean over the stacked axis; optax is a sequential running sum then divide by n in the output dtype (_microbatching.py:190-193), and raises on non-floating outputs (_microbatching.py:69-77) || loop_and_extras: xtrax is lax.scan with no early stop (grad.py:118); optax is lax.fori_loop with num_real_microbatches early stop, SUM/MEAN/RUNNING_MEAN/CONCAT accumulators, transform_fn and metrics_fn (_microbatching.py:439,566-568); neither uses jax.checkpoint (grep: no hits) || argnums: optax can differentiate several arguments (_microbatching.py:557,644); xtrax differentiates only params, the first argument (grad.py:108-112) || filter_spec_unused: xtrax accepts filter_spec but never uses it past the default assignment (grad.py:15,50-51); optax has no equivalent argument",
